Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  05 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  05 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 58 CLINICAL DATA  Left breast mass                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING LOBULAR CARCINOMA  POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3 3   EXTENDING TO THE SURGICAL MARGIN  SEE NOTE  2  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  Note  The tumor mass is 2cm in greatest dimension  Histologically  multiple geographically separate foci of infiltrating tumor are present  The tumor is almost entirely infiltrating  with only a small focus of in situ carcinoma  The infiltrating component has a predominantly alveolar pattern  Lymphatic invasion is present  The alveolar pattern raises the possibility of neuroendocrine differentiation  Positivity of the tumor cells for synaptophysin by immunoperoxidase lends some support to this  However  the tumor is negative for chromogranin  and a Grimelius stain is negative  Diagnosis by  Daniel Rubin  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 14 01                                                                                     HORMONE BINDING ASSAY Addendum     RESULTS OF HORMONE BINDING ASSAYS AS REPORTED BY DAVID T  MACLAUGHLIN  PhD   726  REMOVED_CASE_ID   estrogen receptor  Positive 243 fm mg cytosolic protein progesterone receptor  Positive 61 fm mg cytosolic protein Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 10 34     S PHASE ANALYSIS Addendum     BREAST   LEFT  EXCISION   BRDU UPTAKE  PERCENTAGE OF CELLS IN S PHASE   3   SEE NOTE  NOTE  The breast tumor tissue  after being incubated in medium containing a thymidine analog  bromodeoxyuridine  was processed and stained by immunohistochemical methods to detect those cells which were replicating DNA  Positive cells  cells in S phase  were counted by microscopic visualization of the breast tissue  Results from 372 MGH cases of invasive ductal carcinoma have shown cells in S phase ranging from 0  to 40   with a mean 6 3  and median of 5  Benign lesions  and invasive lobular carcinomas have consistantly shown very low counts  less than 3    Added by  Ann D  Thor  M D  Signed On  12 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 15 20 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast mass  is a 5 0x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm breast biopsy specimen  The external surface is inked and sectioned to reveal a red tan  fleshy  well defined lobular mass with a white rim that measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  It is focally at the margin  Representative section is submitted as frozen section  1 and the frozen block is saved frozen  Tissue is also taken for estrogen receptor studies as well as BRDU studies  The remainder is submitted in A through G  Resident  C  Diana Jordan  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  LEFT BREAST MASS   CARCINOMA  PROBABLY OF DUCTAL ORIGIN  O R  Resident  Jay Austen  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Teri L  Moore  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SURGICAL DAY CARE   ACC 3 REPORTS TO  Charles Mason Ferguson  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST MASS   report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  ACCESSIONED ON  30 REMOVED_MONTH 91 at 14 05 CLINICAL DATA  Metaplastic carcinoma with osteoclastic giant cells  Minor component of typical infiltrating ductal carcinoma mixed with intraductal carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   RIGHT   METAPLASTIC CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Most of the tumor is composed of highly anaplastic spindle and epithelioid cells  accompanied by abundant osteoclast like giant cells  In areas  the malignant spindle cells produce osteoid  A small focus  less than 1  of the total tumor  of intraductal carcinoma of the solid type is present  The accompanying report of immunoperoxidase studies from Rhode Island Hospital states the malignant spindle cells focally  stain positively for keratin and EMA  and do not stain for vimentin  These features are consistent with metaplastic breast carcinoma  It is not possible to assess the resection margins  Vascular invasion is present  Diagnosis by  Teri L  Moore  MD Signed On  31 REMOVED_MONTH 91 at 17 51                                                                                     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     Immunohistochemistry on formalin fixed paraffin embedded tissue shows that the tumor cells are positive for vimentin  muscle specific and smooth muscle specific actin  EMA and alpha 1 antichymotrypsin and are negative for keratin  S 100 and desmin  This staining pattern is consistent with myofibroblastic or smooth muscle differentiation of the tumor cells  Added by  Andrew Eric Rosenberg  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 15                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH OUTSIDE LOCATION REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  OUTSIDE INSTITUTION  RHODE ISLAND HOSPITAL OUTSIDE PATHOLOGIST  M S  Duwaji  M D  RHODE ISLAND HOSPITAL DEPARTMENT OF PATHOLOGY PROVIDENCE  RI  REMOVED_CASE_ID  OUTSIDE CLINICIAN  Norbert J  Craybas  M D  PART   RIGHT BREAST   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Date of Procedure  23 JUL  REMOVED_CASE_ID  Slides  17 Blocks  0   report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
