t necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  21 MAY 03 at 13 01    REVISED REMOVED_DATE        HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF FLUORESCENCE IN SITU HYBRIDIZATION  FISH  FOR HER 2 NEU GENE AMPLIFICATION Breast  Right  block B   HER 2 neu gene in tumor cells  REMOVED_DATE  Not Amplified   See note  Note  Results are expressed as the average ratio of HER 2 to chromosome 17 signals in 60 tumor cell nuclei  A ratio of greater than REMOVED_DATE or equal to REMOVED_DATE indicates  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  neu gene amplification adjusted for chromosome 17 polysomy using PathVysion by Vysis  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  27 MAY 03 at 08 45 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast excision lumpectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm fibrofatty breast tissue with a short suture designating superior and a long suture designating lateral  The anterior aspect is blue inked  the posterior is black inked  the lateral is green inked  the medial is yellow inked  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm well delineated tan white gritty mass which abuts the posterior and comes to within 0 2cm of the medial  0 5cm of the anterior  0 6cm of the lateral  1 0cm of the superior  2 5cm of the inferior margins  The remaining parenchyma is predominantly yellow lobulated fatty tissue admixed with minimal thin white fibrous tissue  Representative sections are submitted sequentially from superior to inferior as follows  A  Uninvolved parenchyma toward superior margin  B D  Tumor to posterior margin  closest  to include anterior margin in D  E  Tumor to medial  second closest  to include anterior  third closest   F  Uninvolved parenchyma toward interior margin  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast final shaved margin superior half of cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of fibrofatty breast tissue fragments which are serially sectioned and entirely submitted as G L  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast final shaved margin inferior half of cavity  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of fibrofatty breast tissue fragments which is serially sectioned and entirely submitted as M Q  Gross Description by  LORI MARINI Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  JHE                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  BREAST RIGHT FINAL SHAVED SUPERIOR REMOVED_DATE CAVITY  EXC PART C  BREAST RIGHT FINAL SHAVED INFERIOR REMOVED_DATE CAVITY  EXC , Moderate_(grade_II).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  11 AUG 98 ACCESSIONED ON  11 AUG 98 at 10 35 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer  biopsied elsewhere  reviewed here  Stitch is superior                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE LOBULAR CARCINOMA  INTERMEDIATE GRADE  DIFFUSELY INFILTRATING THE BREAST  PRESENT IN ELEVEN OF FOURTEEN SLIDES  AND EXTENDING TO REMOVED_DATE CM FROM THE DEEP RESECTION MARGIN  LOBULAR CARCINOMA IN SITU  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   DISSECTION  METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN THIRTEEN OF THIRTEEN LYMPH NODES WITH MODERATE EXTRACAPSULAR TUMOR EXTENSION  Diagnosis by  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD Signed On  14 AUG 98 at 18 06                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  Right   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  04 REMOVED_MONTH 98 at 14 33     HER 2 Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR HER 2 c erb REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Breast  Right   The tumor cells show moderate overexpression of HER 2 c erb 2  See note  Note  This test was developed and its performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  It has not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  28 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 14 07 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number only  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm right modified radical mastectomy with a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm portion of attached axillary tail and a REMOVED_DATE x 4 9cm tan white skin ellipse  The skin ellipse has an eccentric 3 5cm unremarkable nipple areola complex  There is a 3 5cm horizontal  healing surgical incision on the lateral aspect of the skin ellipse located 0 5cm from the closest skin margin  superior margin   The specimen has a suture designating the superior aspect  Sectioning beneath the skin s scar reveals several small biopsy cavities  The first measures REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm and is hemorrhagic  This site is located 0 2cm from the skin margin and 2 5cm from the deep margin  The second identifiable site is located 0 8cm posteriorly from the first site and 1 3cm from the deep margin  Adjacent to the site is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 6cm firm  focally gray white mass which abuts the deep margin  Further sectioning reveals a third site measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm  This site is located 0 5cm from the deep margin  The surrounding tissue is fibrotic and shows areas of fat necrosis  This biopsy site is just superior to the previously mentioned firm mass  The remaining breast parenchyma shows yellow fat and a small amount of soft  gray white fibrous tissue  There is a large area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 6cm of firm  gray white fibrotic tissue with multiple cysts measuring up to 0 5cm in diameter  Multiple lymph nodes are dissected from the axillary tail  ranging in size from 0 2cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  The cut surfaces of the lymph nodes are gray white with tan somehow focal areas of fat  A representative section of each lymph node is submitted  Section code  A  First biopsy cavity to deep margin  B  First biopsy cavity to skin margin  C  First biopsy cavity  D E  Second biopsy site to deep margin  including a portion of firm nodule  F  Additional section of second biopsy site  G  Section of firm nodule to deep margins  H I  Third biopsy site to deep margin  J  Additional section of third biopsy site  K N  Sections of fibrotic area with cysts  O T  Lymph nodes  Gross Description by  PAMELA ROMAN                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Moderate_(grade_II).
