Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  15 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  15 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 16 14 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  OCCUPYING THE WALL OF THE BIOPSY CAVITY AND INVADING LYMPHATIC VESSELS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  EXTENSIVE  EXTENDING TO THE INFERIOR MARGIN OF THE SPECIMEN  HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel invasion is not seen  The margin of the specimen appears free of invasive carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  21 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 07 45                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  25 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 14 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  s name and unit number and  left breast  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm simple mastectomy specimen overlaid by a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm areola entered by a 0 8cm in maximal diameter nipple  The nipple surface is slightly irregular and the nipple appears slightly retracted  The specimen superior half  designated by the surgeon with a short stitch  is inked black  the inferior half is inked blue and the deep resection margin is inked green  The lateral resection margin  designated by the surgeon with a long stitch  is inked yellow  Along the inferior border of the mastectomy is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm skin ellipse  centered by a 2 8cm long  well healed linear scar  Sectioning deeper in this area reveals a REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm biopsy cavity  that extends for an approximate length of 3 5cm  along the inferior resection margin of the specimen  From this area radiate numerous white fibrous bands that reach the resection margin in multiple points  Superior to the biopsy site is an irregular REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm area of white  slightly firm breast parenchyma  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm white  firm area is located in the superolateral portion of the breast  scattered with yellow granules  measuring 0 2cm in maximal diameter  No lymph nodes can be dissected from the superolateral portion of the specimen  Section Code  A D  Biopsy cavity  E  Central area of firmness  F G  Superolateral area area of slight nodularity H  Nipple  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  Michael L Grossbard  M D  Edi Brogi  M D   PhD  PART   BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 ACCESSIONED ON  13 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 18 51 CLINICAL DATA  49 year old female status post right modified radical mastectomy in  REMOVED_CASE_ID  with residual disease  now with left mammographic abnormality  read as infiltrating ductal carcinoma on needle biopsy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL ADENOCARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  SEE NOTE  WITH EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC VASCULAR INVASION AND MULTIFOCAL INVOLVEMENT OF THE BREAST  REMOVED_DATE AXILLARY LYMPH NODES ARE POSITIVE FOR METASTATIC ADENOCARCINOMA  THERE IS EXTENSIVE LYMPHATIC INVOLVEMENT WITHIN THE AXILLARY FAT  NOTE  At least four separate foci of carcinoma are identified in the breast parenchyma  including areas that did not show gross evidence of tumor  Examined inked margins are free of tumor  Because of the multifocal involvement  the absence of an in situ component  and the recent history of metastatic carcinoma elsewhere  we favor the interpretation that this tumor is a metastasis from the right breast primary  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D  Signed On  20 REMOVED_MONTH 93 at 11 33 Consulting Pathologist s   Dennis Sgroi  M D  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D                                                                                  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Left breast  is a left modified radical mastectomy specimen weighing 445 grams  The total specimen measures 25 x 13 x 3 5cm  The breast measures 16 x 13 x 2 5cm and the axillary tail measures 9 x REMOVED_DATE x 1cm  Overlying the specimen is a 17 x 6cm skin ellipse containing the nipple and a 4cm healed scar located inferolaterally to the nipple  Located deep to this scar is a hard nodular  white to yellow area with central hemorrhage  This nodular area measures 4 x 3 x 2cm  It extends to within 0 6cm of the deep margin and 1cm of the inferior margin  Located 7cm medially from the biopsy site and 4cm laterally from the medial resection margin is a 0 5cm hard  tan nodule  This nodule is 1 5cm beneath the skin surface and 2 5cm from the neasest resection margin which is the superior margin  Sectioning of the axillary fat reveals multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 0 4cm  There are also two lymph nodes measuring REMOVED_DATE and the other 1 1cm  Section Code  A E representative sections from the biopsy cavity  F  section demonstrating the relationship of the biopsy site to the deep margin  G  representative sections demonstrating the relationship of the biopsy site to the inferior margin  H  representative sections of biopsy site with overlying skin  I J  the entire nodule from the medial lower quadrant  K  section from the upper medial quadrant  L  section from the medial lower quadrant  M  cystic structure from the outer lower quadrant  N O  nipple in its entirety  P S  axillary lymph nodes  T U  each contain a single large lymph node bisected  V  more axillary lymph nodes  Received separately labeled  Axillary lymph nodes  is a 2 x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm fatty fragment of tissue bisected and submitted entirely  Resident  Lisa H  Lerner  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Herbert Charles Hoover Jr   M D  W B Jerry Younger  M D  Peter Hedberg  M D  PART   LEFT BREAST   report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
