allic clips are identified  Surrounding the cavity is an abundant amount of tan white dense  fibrous tissue  The cavity extends to within 3 1cm of the posterior margin  and 1 4cm of the anterior margin and is located superior to the skin  The remainder of the cut surface consists of lobulated tan yellow adipose tissue with a moderate amount of interspersed gray white fibrous tissue  No other discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified  The lateral aspect of the specimen is palpated and sectioned  lymph nodes are not grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section of biopsy cavity   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue away from biopsy cavity  Received fresh  labeled  right breast   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm right mastectomy specimen with a stitch on the axillary region  which is partially surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm wrinkled  tan nipple and areolar skin with a central 1 5cm in diameter  grossly unremarkable nipple  The posterior margin of the specimen is inked black  the anterior surface inked blue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a lobulated tan yellow fatty cut surface with a moderate amount of interspersed dense gray white fibrous tissue with focal cystic areas consistent with fibrocystic change  No discrete masses or lesions are grossly identified  The lateral aspect of the specimen is palpated  No lymph nodes are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue from the upper outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue from the lower outer quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue from the lower inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue from the upper inner quadrant   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous tissue from the central aspect of the specimen  Received fresh  labeled  right axillary sentinel node   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan yellow to tan pink portion of fat which contains two possible tan pink lymph nodes averaging 1 0cm in greatest dimension  The tissue is sectioned and submitted entirely as follows  SECTION CODE   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One possible lymph node serially sectioned   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   One possible lymph node serially sectioned  Received fresh  labeled  skin left breast   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of multiple irregular  wrinkled portions of grossly unremarkable white skin  No masses or lesions are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Received fresh  labeled  skin right breast   is an REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm aggregate of multiple irregular  grossly unremarkable portions of wrinkled white skin  No masses or lesions are grossly identified  Representative sections are submitted in blocks  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Final Diagnosis by Dennis Sgroi M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY PART C  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   SENTINEL    EXCISION PART D  SKIN  LEFT BREAST   EXCISION PART E  SKIN  RIGHT BREAST   EXCISION  report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  CASE  MS 08  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REMOVED_PATIENT_NAME  Date Taken  REMOVED_DATE Source Care Unit  MGH Inpatient Path Subspecialty Service  Breast 1 Results To  MICHELLE C SPECHT  M D  Resident  Gabrielle Baker  M D  Signed Out by  Ronald Balassanian  M D  CLINICAL DATA  The patient is a 68 year old woman with a history of bilateral invasive ductal carcinoma  undergoing bilateral mastectomies  FINAL DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  RESIDUAL INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  MICROSCOPIC FOCUS  MEASURING REMOVED_DATE CM  2  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE  SEE NOTE  Note  The distance to all margins measures 0 2cm or greater for both ductal carcinoma in situ and invasive ductal carcinoma  The invasive ductal carcinoma is present in the area of the healing biopsy site with dense granulation tissue and fat necrosis  An immunohistochemical stain for cytokeratin cocktail performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  highlights the invasive carcinoma and confirms the diagnosis  BREAST  LEFT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  1  METASTATIC DUCTAL CARCINOMA  PRESENT IN ONE OF TWO INTRAMAMMARY LYMPH NODES  1 1   2  RESIDUAL DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  MICROSCOPIC FOCI  3  HEALING BIOPSY SITE  4  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH FLORID DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  USUAL TYPE AND SCLEROSING ADENOSIS  5  THE DISTANCE TO ALL MARGINS MEASURES REMOVED_DATE CM OR GREATER FOR BOTH DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU AND INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  SEE NOTE  Note  A panel of immunohistochemical stains for cytokeratin  p63  myosin and calponin were performed on slide  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The immunostaining pattern highlights the myoepithelial layer in areas of ductal carcinoma in situ and supports the diagnosis  By his her signature below  the pathologist listed as making the Final Diagnosis certifies that he she has personally reviewed this case and confirmed or corrected the diagnoses  GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received are 2 containers  which are all  labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME   REMOVE_MRN  Received fresh and labeled  right breast   is a 23 x 15 x 3 5cm mastectomy specimen with a suture designating axillary tail  The specimen bears a REMOVED_DATE x 6 5cm skin ellipse with a central 3 x 3 5cm nipple areolar complex  The lateral aspect of the skin ellipse bears a well healed 3 5cm linear defect and immediately subjacent is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm ovoid non healed defect  Deep to the incision site is a poorly defined firm nodularity approximating 5 x 3 x 2cm  The anterior aspect of the specimen is inked blue  the posterior aspect of the specimen is inked black  Located in the superolateral aspect of the specimen is a 3 x 2cm heterogenous firm yellow tan region which extends to the overlying black inked margin  Deep to the well healed incision is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm cavity consistent with prior surgical site  This lesion is centrally hemorrhagic and peripherally firm and yellow tan with focal peripheral yellow orange punctate irregularities  This cavity extends to 0 1cm from the black inked margin and 2 3cm from the blue inked margin  The remaining parenchyma is focally fibrotic but otherwise grossly unremarkable  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavitary lesion to black inked margin   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of cavitary lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavitary lesion with peripheral orange yellow nodularities   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of cavitary lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Fibrous bands extending anteriorly from cavitary lesion   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of fibrous firm region in superolateral aspect of specimen   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections distant from lesion  Received fresh and labeled  left breast   is a 22 x REMOVED_DATE x 3cm mastectomy specimen bearing a REMOVED_DATE x 6 8cm tan pink skin ellipse with a central 3 x 2 5cm nipple areolar complex  The specimen is oriented with a stitch designating axillary tail  There is a well healed curvilinear scar spanning the upper outer quadrants of the areola  The posterior surface is remarkable for a REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm defect overlying a cavitary lesion which is 2 4cm in depth  This cavitation extends to 0 3cm from the anterior margin  The anterior surface is inked blue  the posterior surface is inked black  The specimen is sectioned to reveal focal fibrosis throughout the specimen  The cavitary lesion is lined by hemorrhagic glistening tissue consistent with granulation tissue  The periphery of the lesion is notable for multiple orange yellow punctate nodularities  2 2cm from the inferolateral extent of the cavitary lesion is a heterogenous REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm red tan nodule  Adjacent to the stitch demarcating the axillary tail is a REMOVED_DATE x 1 x 1cm nodule with a tan yellow and focally hemorrhagic cut surface  Sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of axillary nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule adjacent to cavitary lesion  entirely   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Medial aspect of cavitary lesion with orange yellow punctate nodularities   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Cavitation to anterior surface   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative sections of cavitary lesion  black inked margin in  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID     REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Nodule   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Representative section distant to cavitary lesion  Final Diagnosis by Ronald Balassanian M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE PART A  Breast  Right   Simple Mastectomy PART B  Breast  Left   Simple Mastectomy  report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
