Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  24 REMOVED_MONTH 99 ACCESSIONED ON  24 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 10 19 CLINICAL DATA  44 year old white female with invasive ductal carcinoma  status post lumpectomy and axillary dissection  Now for simple mastectomy                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   SIMPLE MASTECTOMY  MICROSCOPIC NESTS OF IN SITU AND INVASIVE CARCINOMA IN HEALING BIOPSY CAVITY WALL  INVASIVE COMPONENT AGGREGATES TO ABOUT REMOVED_DATE CM   SEE NOTE  NOTE  Lymphatic invasion is present  Examined margins are free of carcinoma  Diagnosis by  MARYAM S  MOHAMMADKHANI  MD Signed On  01 REMOVED_MONTH 99 at 17 22                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   is a simple mastectomy specimen  REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm  The overlying skin measures REMOVED_DATE x 11 5cm on which a healed surgical scar measuring 5 0cm in length is identified on the upper outer quadrant  In addition  a 1 0cm healed surgical scar is identified at the axillary apex of the skin  The resection margin is inked black and the specimen serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm cystic cavity filled with blood clot in the upper outer quadrants of the breast  The cavity is 1 2cm from the deep resection margin and 1 8cm from the overlying skin  Areas of fat necrosis are identified adjacent to the cavity  A poorly defined area of gray white fibrosis is identified in the right lower quadrant  measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 0cm  No lymph nodes are identified  SECTION CODE  A B  Cyst cavity with the deep resection margin  C D  Representative sections from cavity wall  E  Area of fibrosis  Resident  VIKRAM DESHPANDE  MD                 