Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 09 19 CLINICAL DATA  Right breast cancer                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE 2  REMOVED_DATE CM  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEE NOTE  NOTE  Blood vessel and lymphatic invasion is not seen  The margins of the specimen appear free of the tumor  LYMPH NODES  RIGHT AXILLA   METASTATIC CARCINOMA IN ONE OF EIGHT LYMPH NODES  SEE NOTE  NOTE  The metastasis is confined to the lymph node  LYMPH NODE  RIGHT AXILLA   HIGHEST    THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN ONE OF ONE LYMPH NODE  Diagnosis by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 15 41                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  10 REMOVED_MONTH 96 at 12 23     IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR C ERB  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  PROTEIN AS REPORTED BY IMPATH BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for c erb  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 MAY 97 at 09 00     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  Staining for hormone receptor proteins was repeated at the patient s request  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  24 MAY 97 at 09 00 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right modified mastectomy  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm unoriented right breast  with a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm skin ellipse with an unremarkable nipple with no incisions  The specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal an ill defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm hemorrhagic area approximately 2 0cm from the skin ellipse  grossly abutting the closest inked surface  Approximately 8 0cm away from the hemorrhagic area is a firm REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm nodule sectioned to reveal an ill defined  stellate hard white mass surrounded by hemorrhage focally extending to within 0 1cm of a deep margin  The remaining parenchyma consists of fibrofatty tissue  with focal areas of hemorrhage  Section Code  A G  representative sections of ill defined hemorrhagic area  H K  representative sections of firm stellate white nodule  L  representative section of firm white areas surrounding biopsy cavity  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Right axillary nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm fragment of adipose tissue  dissected to reveal multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 2cm  Representative sections of lymph nodes submitted in M through P  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  Highest axillary nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm fragment of adipose tissue  dissected to reveal a tan brown lymph node  which is bisected and submitted entirely in cassette Q  Resident  SAHA SADEGHI  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Susan E Briggs  M D  Alisa B  Goldberg M D  PART A  RIGHT MASTECTOMY PART B  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODES PART C  RIGHT AXILLARY LYMPH NODE   HIGHEST    report_end  , Moderate_(grade_II).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 ACCESSIONED ON  26 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 31 CLINICAL DATA  Previous fine needle aspiration showed adenocarcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  98    REMOVED_DATE CM  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  EXTENDING TO WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF THE POSTERIOR RESECTION MARGIN  SEE NOTE   2  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  2    CRIBIFORM TYPE WITH NECROSIS AND ASSOCIATED MICROCALCIFICATIONS  APPROACHING THE INKED SURFACE IN SEVERAL AREAS  BREAST  RIGHT   ADDITIONAL ANTERIOR MARGIN   EXCISION  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  SEVERAL MICROSCOPIC FOCI  PRESENT WITHIN REMOVED_DATE CM OF INKED SURFACE  NOTE  No definite blood vascular or lymphatic invasion is present  Diagnosis by  Andrea Flieder  MD Signed On  30 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 18 02                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 95 at 14 12 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  right breast   are two fragments of fibroadipose breast tissue  with the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm and the smaller measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm  A stitch designates the posterior margin of the largest specimen  A note by the surgeon indicates that the smaller fragment of tissue is additional anterior margin  All specimens are inked black with the posterior surface of the largest specimen inked yellow over black  The additional anterior margin is entirely submitted in cassette A  The largest specimen is sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm ill defined  white to white yellow  firm  nodular area  located in the anterior portion of the largest specimen  within REMOVED_DATE to 0 1cm of the inked resection margin  The nodule has scattered punctate hemorrhage especially at its periphery  The remaining parenchyma is mostly adipose tissue  and unremarkable  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes B through J  with the nodule in cassettes B through D  Resident  EDI BROGI  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  08 MAY 95 ACCESSIONED ON  08 MAY 95 at 15 14 CLINICAL DATA  MGH  fine needle biopsy diagnosis carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MASTECTOMY  1  INFILTRATING DUCTAL CARCINOMA  99    6 CM IN DIAMETER   POORLY DIFFERENTIATED  GRADE 3 3  AND FOCAL INTRADUCTAL CARCINOMA  1    2  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 8 OF 8 AXILLARY LYMPH NODES  NOTE  Focal lymphatic invasion is identified  All resection margins are negative for carcinoma  the closest one is inferior and measures 0 5cm  LYMPH NODES  LEVEL ONE  RIGHT   LYMPHADENECTOMY  FIBROFATTY TISSUE  NO LYMPH NODES IDENTIFIED  SKIN  2 O CLOCK   BIOPSY  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITIES RECOGNIZED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  SKIN  4 O CLOCK   BIOPSY  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITIES RECOGNIZED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  SKIN  6 O CLOCK   BIOPSY  NO DIAGNOSTIC ABNORMALITIES RECOGNIZED  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  THE FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS IS CONFIRMED  Diagnosis by  Gunnlaugur P  Nielsen  MD Signed On  12 MAY 95 at 18 52                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     BREAST  RIGHT   The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  THE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR PROGESTERONE RECEPTOR PROTEIN ARE FOR INVESTIGATIONAL USE ONLY  THEY MUST NOT BE USED FOR CLINICAL PURPOSES  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  23 MAY 95 at 07 15 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  are three separate specimens  Labeled  2 o clock   is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm ellipse of skin  excised to a depth of 0 5cm  entirely frozen as FX 1 and submitted in A  Labeled  4 o clock   is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm ellipse of skin  excised to a depth of 0 4cm  entirely frozen as FX 2 and submitted in B  Labeled  6 o clock   is a REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm ellipse of skin  excised to a depth of 0 4cm  entirely frozen as FX 3 and submitted in C   ADDON AJA  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 10 0cm mastectomy specimen with a REMOVED_DATE x 15 0cm  tan brown  overlying skin ellipse coating a 4 5cm in diameter areola and 1 5cm in diameter nipple  A REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm mass protrudes the skin surface 2 0cm lateral and slightly inferior to the nipple  The skin overlying this mass is dark brown to black in color  and is focally enfoliated  Specimen is inked and sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 6 0cm well circumscribed tan yellow mass abutting the skin and extending to within 0 6cm of the deep resection margin  The remaining breast parenchyma is yellow tan  fibrofatty  and grossly unremarkable  The axillary tail is dissected to reveal eight tan brown lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm  to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm  SECTION CODE  U  Closest approach of tumor to deep resection margin  V  Closest approach of tumor to skin  D J and W  Representative sections through tumor  K  Medial most margin  L  Lateral most margin M  Representative section of nipple  N P  One axillary lymph node each  Q  Two axillary lymph nodes  R  Three axillary lymph nodes  Received  labeled   level one nodes  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 8cm piece of yellow tan  fibrofatty tissue containing no definite lymph nodes  Submitted entirely in S and T  Gross Description by  FANG FANG  MD  PhD Resident  Ajit J  Alles  MD  PhD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  1  2 O CLOCK  SKIN AND SUBCUTANEOUS TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  2  4 O CLOCK  SKIN AND SUBCUTANEOUS TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  FROZEN SECTION DIAGNOSIS  3  6 O CLOCK  SKIN AND SUBCUTANEOUS TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  O R  Resident  Robin E  Kirby  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Austin L  Vickery  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Kenneth Kenji Tanabe  M D  PART A  SKIN  2 O CLOCK  PART B  SKIN  4 O CLOCK  PART C  SKIN  6 O CLOCK  PART D  BREAST AXILLARY  RIGHT  PART E  LYMPH NODES  LEVEL ONE  RIGHT    report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
