cs determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Atul Kumar Bhan  M D  Signed On  18 REMOVED_MONTH 01 at 16 23 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  right breast and axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 0cm modified radical mastectomy surfaced by a REMOVED_DATE x 4 5cm elliptical skin with a 2 5cm linear scar located 2 5cm from an unremarkable nipple  The specimen is inked and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm ill defined fibrous area located 1 5cm from the posterior margin  Representative sections of the tissue surrounding this area is submitted as A D  with A C containing the nearest posterior inked margin  There is also a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm tan white firm irregular area located 1 0cm from the posterior margin and 4 0cm away from the first fibrous area  and representative sections are submitted as E and F  Cassette G contains a representative section of grossly unremarkable breast tissue  Additional firm parenchyma from the lateral portion of the breast is submitted in H and P Q  anterior margin overinked blue   There is an attached REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 3 0cm axillary tail containing multiple lymph nodes  of which representative sections are submitted as I O  Resident  ARASH RADFAR  MD  PhD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART   BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY   report_end  , Moderate_(grade_II).
