ration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  27 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 16 19 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh in the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast  is a left mastectomy specimen with short stitch superior long stitch lateral measuring 16 x 15 x 2 5cm with an REMOVED_DATE 5 x REMOVED_DATE axillary tail  and a REMOVED_DATE x 3 5cm tan white skin ellipse containing nipple and areola complex  Superior to the nipple is a healing and linear incision measuring 2 5cm  The specimen is inked in black and serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm well circumscribed mass with small yellow punctate areas of necrosis  This mass is adjacent to a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 4cm biopsy site  The mass is 0 5cm from the posterior margin  The mass and biopsy tract are located in the upper inner quadrant of the left breast  Section Code  A D  mass in its entirety and biopsy cavity  with closest margin in A  There is an additional REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 7cm firm white area with foci of yellow necrosis  This area is 1 9cm from the anterior skin margin and 1 2cm from the posterior deep margin  This mass is 0 4cm anterior and 0 2cm inferior to the above biopsy tract and mass  and it is within the upper inner quadrant  Representative sections of this second mass are submitted in E G with the closest the posterior deep margin in G  A representative section of fibrous breast parenchyma from the lower outer quadrant is submitted in H  The axilla tail is separated from the specimen and dissected to reveal multiple focally matted lymph nodes  the largest measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 4cm  Multiple lymph nodes are submitted in I N  A single larger lymph node is bivalved and submitted in entirety in O and the large