suring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm  It is 0 5cm from the anterior  0 6cm from the lateral  0 8cm from the posterior  1 5cm from the superior  2 8cm from the medial  and 4 5cm from the inferior margins  The remaining uninvolved parenchyma consists of tan white fibrotic tissue and yellow  focally hemorrhagic and lobulated fat  Representative sections are submitted as follows   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The entire superior mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The entire inferior mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   The entire anterolateral mass   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Intervening parenchyma between the superior and the inferior mass with the aspect closest to the superior mass inked orange  not a margin    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Uninvolved parenchyma  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast lymph node  suspicious    are REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm in aggregate of yellow  lobulated fat which contains four potential lymph nodes ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 1cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm which are entirely submitted in cassette  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID   Gross Dictation by Rebecca J DiIorio  on REMOVED_DATE Micro Dx Dictation by Jennifer Nash  on REMOVED_DATE Final Diagnosis by Melinda J Lerwill M D   Electronically signed on REMOVED_DATE RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left  block  REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID    The tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The tumor cells do not show overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s ac