Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  FinalType  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  10 AUG 99 ACCESSIONED ON  10 AUG 99 at 11 00 CLINICAL DATA  Invasive and intraductal breast carcinoma                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  LEFT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE SEE NOTE  LYMPH NODES 18 OF 18 LYMPH NODES NEGATIVE FOR METASTATIC CARCINOMA  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE    EXCISION  MICROSCOPIC METASTATIC CARCINOMA  PRESENT IN ONE OF SIX LYMPH NODES  BREAST  LEFT   ADDITIONAL LATERAL TISSUE    EXCISION  FIBROFATTY TISSUE WITH SKELETAL MUSCLE  NOTE  Carcinoma in situ extensively involves an area measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 2cm and is greater than 0 2cm from all resection margins  Although no definite stromal invasion is identified  there are scattered suspicious areas that likely represent early microinvasion  This interpretation is in keeping with the finding of a micrometastasis of carcinoma present in a single lymph node in the separately submitted additional axillary tissue  Diagnosis by  RHONDA YANTISS  MD Signed On  16 AUG 99 at 19 12                                                                                     BREAST CANCER IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY ADDENDUM Addendum     RESULTS OF IMMUNOHISTOCHEMICAL STAINING FOR RECEPTOR PROTEINS Breast  Left   The noninvasive tumor cells do not stain for estrogen receptor protein  The noninvasive tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  The noninvasive tumor cells show strong overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  The sections stained for receptor proteins do not contain invasive carcinoma  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  06 REMOVED_MONTH 00 at 08 29 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  left breast and axillary contents  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 5 5cm modified radical mastectomy with yellow  fibrofatty piece of tissue that has already been sliced to reveal a firm pink tan  gritty parenchyma within the soft fat  Specimen includes a REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm skin ellipse with nipple that is pink tan in color  A 5 5cm curvilinear scar is noted superior to the nipple  Upon sectioning  there is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 4 2cm ill defined gritty firm pink white tan mass with punctate plaques associated with it  The mass is 0 7cm from the anterior margin  1 0cm from the posterior margin  1 0cm from the superior margin  8 0cm from the inferior margin  6 0cm from the lateral margin and 4 3cm from the medial margin  Posterior  anterior and superior margins are taken and submitted in A B and C respectively  The mass is predominantly in the upper outer quadrant with extension into the upper inner and lower outer quadrants  The lower inner quadrant appears free of the mass  Representative sections of the mass from the upper outer quadrant are submitted in D H  Representative sections of lower inner quadrant are in I  Representative sections from upper inner quadrant are in J  Representative sections from lower outer quadrant are in K  The axillary content is removed from the main specimen and multiple lymph nodes are ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm in L U  Additional sections from the midportion of the mass are submitted in CC HH  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional axillary tissue  are multiple fragments of tan  yellow  firm  irregular  fibrofatty tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm in aggregate  Multiple lymph nodes are ranging from REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 3cm to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 2cm dissected and placed in V X  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  Additional lateral tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm yellow tan  fibrofatty  irregular shaped piece of tissue  Specimen is sectioned to reveal a yellow  lobulated  fibrofatty cut surface  Specimen is submitted in entirety in cassette Y BB  Section code  A  Posterior margin B  Anterior margin C  Superior margin D H  Upper outer quadrant representative sections of mass I  Representative sections from left inner quadrant J  Representative sections from upper inner quadrant K  Representative sections from lower outer quadrant L X  Lymph node Y BB  Additional lateral tissue  CC HH  Additional sections of mass from main specimen The axillary tail is removed from the main breast specimen and multiple lymph nodes are dissected out and submitted in cassettes L through U  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional axillary tissue  are multiple fragments of tan yellow  firm  irregular  fibrofatty pieces of tissue measuring REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2cm in aggregate  Multiple lymph nodes are dissected and placed in V through X  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional lateral tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 9cm yellow tan  fibrofatty  irregular shaved piece of tissue  The specimen is sectioned to reveal a yellow  lobulated  fibrofatty cut surface  The specimen is submitted entirely in cassettes Y through BB  Resident  JOHN BISSONNETTE  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     O R  Diagnosis by  Dennis Sgroi  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  Michael J Yaremchuk  M D  Dennis C Sgroi  M D  PART A  BREAST  LEFT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  BREAST LEFT  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY TISSUE   EXCISION PART C  BREAST  LEFT  ADDITIONAL LATERAL TISSUE   EXCISION   report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 ACCESSIONED ON  16 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 54 CLINICAL DATA   None Provided                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST MASS  LEFT   WIDE EXCISION  INVASIVE DUCTAL CARCINOMA  GRADE REMOVED_DATE  REMOVED_DATE CM IN GREATEST DIMENSION  AS MEASURED FROM A GLASS SLIDE  WITH CENTRAL HYALINIZING FIBROSIS AND NECROSIS  DUCTAL CARCINOMA IN SITU  HIGH GRADE WITHIN AND EXTENDING AWAY FROM THE MASS  LYMPH NODES   LEFT AXILLA  DISSECTION  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 15 OUT OF 15 LYMPH NODES  LYMPH NODES  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY LEFT   TISSUE  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY IN 6 OUT OF 6 LYMPH NODES  BREAST  ADDITIONAL DEEP   RE EXCISION  BREAST TISSUE WITH STROMAL FIBROSIS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  BREAST  ADDITIONAL INFERIOR TO DEEP MARGIN   CAUTERIZED BREAST TISSUE WITH INVOLUTIONAL CHANGE AND FOCAL MICROCALIFICATIONS  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF MALIGNANCY  NOTE  No definite lymphatic or blood vascular invasion is seen  although several suspicious foci are identified  The examined margin of resection appears free of carcinoma  Diagnosis by  Robin E  Kirby  MD Signed On  23 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 17 01                                                                                     RECEPTOR IMMUNOHISTOCHEMISTRY Addendum     RESULTS OF STAINING OF FIXED TISSUE FOR HORMONE RECEPTOR PROTEINS BREAST  LEFT   The tumor cells stain for estrogen receptor protein  The tumor cells do not stain for progesterone receptor protein  See Note  Note  In this laboratory  we used this antibody to stain 100 breast carcinomas prepared in the usual way  paraffin sections  and we compared the results with determinations of estrogen receptor by biochemical assay  91  of tumors that stained with this antibody were positive for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  96  of tumors that failed to stain with this antibody were negative for estrogen receptors by biochemical assay  When we compared the results of staining of paraffin sections with the results of staining of frozen sections  the predictive value of a positive result was 97  and the predictive value of a negative result was 95   In this laboratory  we also compared the results of staining of 100 routinely processed breast carcinomas with determinations of progesterone receptors by a hormone binding assay  Sixty five percent of tumors that stained with this antibody contained progesterone receptors by the biochemical assay  and 98  of tumors that failed to stain lacked the receptors  Added by  Frederick Carl Koerner  M D  Signed On  26 REMOVED_MONTH 97 at 08 30 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received in multiple parts  Labeled  wide excision  left breast  and received fresh from the Frozen Section Lab   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  There is a short stitch and a long stitch designating the superior and the lateral margins resectively  The superior margin is inked in green and lateral in red  The specimen is serially sectioned to reveal a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 5cm firm  ill defined nodule  present at 0 2cm from the closest inferior margin  A representative section of the nodule and inferior margin is frozen as FX 1 and resubmitted in cassette A  B to D are tumor with additional inferior margins  E to H are sections of superior margin  I and J are sections of the lateral and medial margins submitted en face  Labeled  left axillary contents  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 0cm piece of fatty tissue are multiple lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 2 0cm in maximum dimension and disected from this fatty tissue which is submitted in cassettes K V  Cassettes M V contain half of each lymph node  Labeled  additional axillary tissue  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm piece of fatty tissue  Six lymph nodes ranging in size from REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm and disected from this fatty tissue  The lymph nodes are submitted entirely in cassettes Q and R  Labeled  additional  superior and deep margin excision  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 2cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  No mass is identified  Representative sections are submitted in cassettes S T and U  Labeled  additional  inferior to deep margin  and consists of a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm piece of fibrofatty tissue  No lesion is identified  The specimen is entirely submitted in cassettes V and W  Resident  Navneet Narula  MD     INTRA OPERATIVE DIAGNOSIS     FROZEN SECITON DIAGNOSIS  BREAST  LEFT   INFILTRAITING CARCINOMA  MARGINS FREE OF TUMOR  O R  Resident  HENRY DONG  MD O R  Diagnosis by  Nancy Lee Harris  M D                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Barbara Lynn Smith  M D  PART A  BREAST MASS  LEFT   WIDE EXCISION PART B  AXILLARY  LEFT   CONTENTS PART C  ADDITIONAL AXILLARY  LEFT   TISSUE PART D  ADDITIONAL DEEP  RE EXCISION PART E  ADDITIONAL INFERIOR TO DEEP MARGIN   report_end  , Poor_(grade_III).
