Accession Number   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  Report Status  Final Type  Surgical Pathology Pathology Report   REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  OPERATION DATE  19 REMOVED_MONTH 94 ACCESSIONED ON  19 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 20 CLINICAL DATA  69 year old woman with breast carcinoma  positive family history  She is status post biopsy showing infiltrating ductal carcinoma grade I III on the right breast                                                                                      FINAL DIAGNOSIS     BREAST  RIGHT   MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY  1  NO RESIDUAL CARCINOMA  2  FIBROCYSTIC CHANGE WITH ATYPICAL EPITHELIAL DUCTAL HYPERPLASIA  MARGINS CLEAR OF ATYPICAL HYPERPLASIA  3  BIOPSY SITE WITH FIBROSIS  FAT NECROSIS  CHRONIC INFLAMMATION AND FOREIGN BODY GIANT CELL REACTION  4  THERE IS NO EVIDENCE OF METASTASES IN 10 OF 10 LYMPH NODES EXAMINED  Diagnosis by  Kathleen K  Hansen  MD Signed On  22 REMOVED_MONTH 94 at 15 29                                                                                 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received labeled  right breast and axillary nodes  is a 25 x 20 x 5cm   REMOVED_CASE_ID  gram radical mastectomy specimen with an 11 x 7 x 2 0cm axillary tail and an overlying 24 x 10cm skin ellipse with a centrally located 0 5cm in diameter nipple  The skin ellipse contains recently sutured healing biopsy sites  The first biopsy site is a 5cm scar  located 3cm medially from the nipple  The second site is a 3cm partially healed  sutured scar located 3cm lateral to the nipple  The breast is inked and sectioned to reveal two biopsy cavities lying immediately beneath and corresponding to the skin biopsy sites described above  Biopsy site  1 consists of a 4 x 3 x 1 5cm  partially hemorrhage filled  circumscribed cavity  3cm from the deep margin and 1cm from the skin margin  Biopsy site  2 measures 3 x REMOVED_DATE x 2 5cm and is 4cm from the deep resection margin and 0 5cm from the overlying skin biopsy site  There are two 0 5cm diameter  tan white nodules adjacent to biopsy site  2  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is yellow tan  fibrofatty tissue with occasional areas of fibrosis measuring REMOVED_DATE to 1 0cm  SECTION CODE  A  Representative section  biopsy site  1  closest deep resection margin  B E  Representative sections of biopsy site  1  D and E including skin  F  Closest deep resection margin  biopsy site  2  G J  Representative sections of biopsy site  2  KandL  Representative sections of firm breast nodules adjacent to biopsy site  2  M  Representative section of normal breast  N R  Representative sections of axillary nodes  Resident  Simon Bergman  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Edwin Lee Carter  M D  Janey Sue Pratt  M D  PART   BREAST and AXILLARY NODES  RIGHT    report_end  , Well_differentiated_(grade_I).
