otein  The tumor cells show strong  3   overexpression of HER 2 c erbB 2  See note  Note  These tests were developed and their performance characteristics determined by the Pathology Department at the Massachusetts General Hospital  They have not been cleared or approved by the U S  Food and Drug Administration  FDA   The FDA has determined that such clearance or approval is not necessary  this laboratory has established and verified the test s accuracy and precision  Added by  Grace T  McKee MD Signed On  17 REMOVED_MONTH 03 at 08 27 GROSS DESCRIPTION  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  left breast   is a lumpectomy specimen measuring 11 x 10 x 4cm  oriented by the surgeon as follows  short stitch anterior  long stitch lateral  bowtie cephalad  The specimen is inked as follows  posterior black  anterior blue  superior green  and inferior yellow  The specimen is then serially sectioned to reveal a tan white  firm  irregular but well defined REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 2 2cm mass with an eccentric 0 4cm area of hemorrhage  consistent with needle tract  The mass also contains focal areas of calcification measuring up to 0 2cm  The mass comes to 0 4cm of the closest posterior margin  2cm to the anterior margin  2cm to the superior margin  2 3cm to the inferior margin  2cm to the lateral margin  and 4 5cm to the medial margin  The remainder of the breast parenchyma is examined  and consists of predominantly fatty tissue  with focal fibrous areas  There is one concentrated area of fibrosis measuring REMOVED_DATE x 1 3cm  that abuts the inferior margin  Representative sections of the specimen are submitted as follows  A  Mass to deep and superior margins  B D  Further representative sections of mass  E  Representative section of areas increased fibrosis adjacent to inferior margin  F  Representative section of tissue away from mass  Received fresh   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  primary sentinel node  164   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue containing lymph node  The fat is dissected away to reveal a 1 3cm in greatest dimension lymph node  which is serially sectioned  and submitted in G and H  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  secondary sentinel node  109   is a 2 x 2 x 0 9cm portion of fatty tissue  sectioned to reveal a 1 8cm in greatest dimension lymph node  The fat is dissected away and the lymph node is submitted in I through J  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name and unit number  and  additional tissue  0   is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 5cm portion of fibroadipose tissue  sectioned to reveal unremarkable fibroadipose tissue  No node is identified  The specimen is unoriented  and submitted entirely in K and L  Resident  ALIYAH RAHEMTULLAH  MD                                                                                 SOURCE CARE UNIT  SAME DAY SURGICAL UNIT    REMOVED_ACCESSION_ID  REPORTS TO  Kevin S  Hughes  M D  PART A  BREAST LEFT  EXCISIONAL BIOPSY PART B  LYMPH NODE  PRIMARY SENTINEL  164   EXCISION PART C  LYMPH NODE  SECONDARY SENTINEL  109   EXCISION PART D  BREAST  LEFT   EXCISIONAL BIOPSY , Poor_(grade_III).
