om the posterior  2 0cm from the anterior  5 5cm from the superior  7 0cm from the inferior  5 5cm from the medial  and approximately 20 0cm from the lateral margin  The remaining cut surface is tan yellow lobulated  focally hemorrhagic fibrofatty breast tissue  There are multiple lymph nodes dissected from the axillary tail ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm  Representative sections of the breast and masses and the entire lymph nodes are submitted as follows  A C  Representative sections of the first described mass  D  Representative section of posterior margin subjacent to the first mentioned mass  E  Representative section of second mentioned mass to the posterior resection margin  F H  Additional representative sections of second mentioned mass  I J  Representative sections of fibrous tissue away from the masses  K M  One serially sectioned lymph node  N P  One bisected lymph node each  Q T  Whole lymph nodes  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  highest axillary node  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm tan pink lymph node with a minimal amount of attached tan yellow fat  The specimen is bisected and entirely submitted in cassette U  Received in formalin   labeled REMOVE_PATIENT_NAME  patient s name  unit number  and  additional axillary tissue  is a REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 1 0cm aggregate of lymph node bearing tan yellow adipose tissue  There are multiple lymph nodes dissected out ranging from REMOVED_DATE to REMOVED_DATE x REMOVED_DATE x 0 6cm  The lymph nodes are entirely submitted as follows  V  One bisected lymph node  W  Whole lymph nodes  Gross Description by  JAMES BARRY Resident  RESIDENT FREE SERVICE  FCK                                                                                  SOURCE CARE UNIT  MGH INPATIENT  FLR UNKNOWN  REPORTS TO  Michele Annette Gadd  M D  PART A  BREAST RIGHT  MODIFIED RADICAL MASTECTOMY PART B  LYMPH NODE RIGHT HIGHEST AXILLA  DISSE